  "state_rules": {
    "ordering": ["MAP_OBJECT", "ALLOC_KERNARG", "v1 MEMORY_COPY_H2D", "SUBMIT_AQL", "type-20 completion", "UNMAP_OBJECT"],
    "publication_order": "MAP_OBJECT -> ALLOC_KERNARG -> existing v1 MEMORY_COPY_H2D -> SUBMIT_AQL -> type-20 completion -> UNMAP_OBJECT. MEMORY_COPY_H2D is a v1 carrier, not a new v2 opcode.",
    "ownership": "Every nonzero object, mapping, queue, allocation, signal, ticket, and generation is connection/owner scoped. Stale or cross-owner generations are rejected before publication.",
    "aql": "SUBMIT_AQL contains launch metadata only. The live daemon owns packet materialization, kernel_object, kernarg VA, completion signal linkage, publication, nonzero packet CRC, and lifecycle ticks. Bit 8 records native control admission/retire. When bit 9 is selected, the daemon attaches the execution adapter only after durable type-19, issues one exact locked fixture through GPUDispatcher/ComputeUnit, and emits type-20 only after physical retirement.",
    "memory": "The v2 schema does not make public simulated_va packet-visible by itself. CP25 separates the requested logical kernel ABI alignment from hidden page-backed allocation: logical alignment 8 is returned on wire while the owner-session-fixed 4096/65536 page backing remains private. The live v1 MEMORY_COPY_H2D route publishes the exact owner allocation subrange.",
    "completion_ordering": "packet_crc32c and admission_tick are nonzero; admission_tick <= start_tick <= end_tick <= retire_tick. Bit-8-only type-20 output_crc32c is zero; bit-9 execution type-20 output_crc32c is nonzero and oracle-checked. The current route may set start, end, and retire to the same tick after durable ACK.",
    "execution_session": "At most one execution may be issued per owner/session. A second SUBMIT is rejected before pinning or issue (focused gate second_submit_issue_count=0). Duplicate D2H reads are idempotent and cannot duplicate completion latches.",
    "disconnect": "A disconnect after type-19 and submission quarantines the in-flight task until retire, then releases queue, signal, adapter, pins, and private state without sending type-20 to the disconnected owner. Pre-SUBMIT lease cleanup and normal completed-session cleanup are separate paths.",
    "signal_scope": "The wire expected_signal_value_bits field remains 1 and no wire after-value is observed. Trace signal_before=1/signal_after=0 is the private native AQL completion signal, not a wire post-value.",
    "fetch_rollback": "If CP admission rejects a locally fetched packet, CP23 cancelFetch restores the queue slot before mapping/kernarg pins are released. Admission success records ownership and queue state only unless bit 9's exact execution gate is selected."
  },
